  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Media and Civil Society Strengthening (MACSS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Mongolia):  USAID&apos;s Media and Civil Society Strengthening (MACSS) activity will bolster meaningful citizen participation in Mongolia&apos;s democracy by strengthening social accountability mechanisms (mechanisms that citizens can exercise to hold the state accountable); and improving public access to information vital to democratic political participation. Four pathways will help achieve these results: 1) improving the capacity of civil society organizations; 2) expanding civic space; 3) investing in the investigative journalism capacity of media organizations; and 4) improving effectiveness in countering political disinformation. Interventions will advance transparency and accountability, civic engagement, and ultimately citizen demand for better democratic governance. USAID will strengthen the effectiveness of local civil society organizations (CSO) through greater participation of marginalized and underrepresented groups. Interventions will also open opportunities to ensure diversity in CSO leadership and representation. . ..</narrative>
  </description>
